        "section": "asyncio-task",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "When using this factory (via \"loop.set_task_factory(asyncio.eager_task_factory)\"), coroutines begin execution synchronously during \"Task\" construction. Tasks are only scheduled on the event loop if they block. This can be a performance improvement as the overhead of loop scheduling is avoided for coroutines that complete synchronously.",
        "title": "asyncio-task"
      },
      {
        "end": 545,
        "estimated_tokens": 75,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 2,
        "position": 2,
        "record_id": "51f0e3fed62c12bb09a3582e",
        "score": 0.39470364447885925,
        "section": "asyncio-task",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 307,
        "text": "An optional keyword-only *context* argument allows specifying a custom \"contextvars.Context\" for the *coro* to run in. If no *context* is provided, the Task copies the current context and later runs its coroutine in the copied context.",
        "title": "asyncio-task"
      },
      {
        "end": 824,
        "estimated_tokens": 53,
        "kind": "sentence",
        "page_id": 2,
        "position": 4,
        "record_id": "51f0e3fed62c12bb09a3582e",
        "score": 0.3913703111455259,
        "section": "asyncio-task",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 677,
        "text": "If set to \"True\" and the event loop is running, the task will start executing the coroutine immediately, until the first time the coroutine blocks.",
        "title": "asyncio-task"
      },
      {
        "end": 954,
        "estimated_tokens": 49,
        "kind": "sentence",
        "page_id": 2,
        "position": 5,
        "record_id": "51f0e3fed62c12bb09a3582e",
        "score": 0.39053697781219254,
        "section": "asyncio-task",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 824,
        "text": "If the coroutine returns or raises without blocking, the task will be finished eagerly and will skip scheduling to the event loop.",
        "title": "asyncio-task"
      },
      {
        "end": 645,
        "estimated_tokens": 67,
        "kind": "code_block",
        "page_id": 1,
        "position": 2,
        "record_id": "1698ac52a0f187de4a78f34d",
        "score": 0.38043481488668124,
        "section": "a-conceptual-overview-of-asyncio",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 483,
        "text": "coroutine = loudmouth_penguin(magic_number=5) # This creates a Task object and schedules its execution via the event loop. task = asyncio.create_task(coroutine)",
        "title": "a-conceptual-overview-of-asyncio"
      },
      {
        "end": 659,
